   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to exempting\nthe Bushnell's Basin Fire Department from the forty-five percent limit on\nnon-resident members",
    "basePrintNo": "S9030",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9030-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1402, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9030\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to\nexempting the Bushnell's Basin Fire Department from the forty-five\npercent limit on non-resident members\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow the Bushnell Basin Fire Department to have enough members to\noperate the department and still qualify for the Not-For-Profit Fire\nCompany benefits.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill adds the Bushnell Basin Fire Department to be\nexempt from the forty five percent non-resident member limit.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Bushnell Basin Fire Department serves the hamlet of Bushnell Basin\nwithin the Town of Perinton, Monroe County, New York. Bushnell Basin is\none of the smallest hamlets within Monroe County, and one of the small-\nest Fire Districts. Their current challenge is trying to stay below the\nforty-five percent non-resident member limit imposed under the Not-For-\nProfit Corporation law, while still being able to serve and protect\ntheir community. Amending the Not-For-Profit Corporation Law to include\nthe Bushnell Basin Fire Department in the Fire Companies within the\nexempted companies to the forty-five percent non-resident member limit\nwould allow the proper addition of volunteers from surrounding communi-\nties to guarantee the continued fire safety of Bushnell Basin.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
